// # Library Split Minimum-Viable — Three Oversized Std Files
//
// Logline: 1 door + 1 sibling for each of btree_disk_ops, protein_translation, dispatch_worker. Smallest cut under 256 lines.
//
// Setup: Full split in handoff_library_split.oot (audit/): btree 1+4, protein 1+5, dispatch 1+3. This spec is the 1+1 waypoint. Library lane owns std/*.oo edits; audit lane owns boards.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Per-file minimum cut with line budgets and file:line evidence.
//   2. Function grouping in door vs sibling, and what it sacrifices.
//   3. Reversibility path from 1+1 to the full split.
//   4. Acceptance and BLOCKED-status invariant.

// ## 0. Why minimum-viable
//
// FORMAT.oot:20: "Line limit: Every `.oo` and `.oot` file must not exceed 256 lines. Comments count."
// FORMAT.oot:56: "256-line constraint: Comments count toward the 256-line limit. Split files only along natural domain seams."
// handoff_library_split.oot:21: the three target files are 395, 380, 323 lines.
// Ship-now principle: a less-than-ideal split that ships beats a perfect split that never lands.
// Full split is the destination; 1+1 is the waypoint.

// ## 1. btree_disk_ops.oo (395 lines, cut >= 139)
//
// Source: ooda/std/database/btree_disk_ops.oo.
//
// Current shape (file:line):
//   Lines 1-12    Academy header.
//   Line 13       import "./btree_disk_types.oo";.
//   Lines 15-29   btree_node_key_at (15 lines, slot accessor).
//   Lines 31-45   btree_node_val_at (15 lines, slot accessor).
//   Lines 47-58   btree_node_find_key_index (12 lines).
//   Lines 60-74   btree_node_lookup_value (15 lines).
//   Lines 76-225  btree_node_insert_key_value (150 lines, n=0/1/2/3 cases).
//   Lines 227-300 btree_node_split_leaf (74 lines).
//   Lines 302-395 btree_node_remove_key (94 lines).
//
// Minimum cut: 1 door + 1 sibling.
//
// | File                              | Role              | Lines  | Budget |
// |-----------------------------------|-------------------|--------|--------|
// | btree_disk_ops.oo (door)          | read + insert     | 225    | <=256  |
// | btree_disk_ops_mutate.oo          | split + remove    | ~182   | <=256  |
//
// Door (lines 1-225): header + import + 4 read fns + btree_node_insert_key_value.
// Sibling body (lines 227-395): btree_node_split_leaf + btree_node_remove_key.
// Sibling file = 12 (4-element header) + 1 (import) + 169 (body) = 182 lines.
//
// Function grouping: door = read paths + the primary write (insert). Sibling = the
// two lifecycle ops (split, remove). Both siblings depend on BTreeNode and BTreeSplit
// from btree_disk_types.oo:24-58 and :60-74, so the import is shared. No new imports introduced.
//
// Trade-off vs full split (1+4 in handoff_library_split.oot:54-66):
//   - Door mixes read fns with insert. The full split gives insert its own sibling.
//   - Sibling bundles split and remove. The full split gives each its own sibling.
//   - Cross-sibling calls: none. insert, split, remove are independent operations
//     on BTreeNode; none calls another.
//
// Reversibility: subdivide the sibling into btree_disk_ops_split.oo (~89 lines) and
// btree_disk_ops_remove.oo (~109 lines) per handoff_library_split.oot:60-62. Door
// stays. Optionally further split insert out of the door. Net: 1+1 -> 1+3 (or 1+4).

// ## 2. protein_translation.oo (380 lines, cut >= 124)
//
// Source: ooda/std/bioinformatics/protein_translation.oo.
//
// Current shape (file:line):
//   Lines 1-12    Academy header.
//   Lines 14-20   type ProteinSequence.
//   Lines 22-29   type OrfRecord.
//   Lines 31-38   type TranslateAcc.
//   Lines 40-52   int_pow4, int_pow32.
//   Lines 54-72   dna_base_at, dna_pack4, codon_pack, codon_at.
//   Lines 74-175  codon_standard_aa (102 lines, NCBI table 1).
//   Lines 177-195 codon_is_start_standard, codon_is_stop_standard.
//   Lines 197-262 protein_aa_weight_da (66 lines, residue masses).
//   Lines 264-278 protein_aa_charge.
//   Lines 280-338 translate_empty, translate_scan, protein_translate_frame,
//                  protein_translate_nucleotides, protein_estimate_molecular_weight,
//                  protein_estimate_net_charge.
//   Lines 340-380 protein_sequence_new, protein_sequence_mw, protein_sequence_charge,
//                  protein_orf_new, orf_is_complete.
//
// Minimum cut: 1 door + 1 sibling.
//
// | File                                    | Role              | Lines  | Budget |
// |-----------------------------------------|-------------------|--------|--------|
// | protein_translation.oo (door)           | types + scan      | ~173   | <=256  |
// | protein_translation_lookup.oo           | codon + AA props  | ~217   | <=256  |
//
// Door (lines 1-72 + 280-380): header + 3 types + pack utils + translate_* +
// protein_sequence_* + protein_orf_new + orf_is_complete.
// Sibling body (lines 74-278): codon_standard_aa + codon_is_start_standard +
// codon_is_stop_standard + protein_aa_weight_da + protein_aa_charge.
// Sibling file = 12 (4-element header) + 205 (body) = 217 lines. No imports.
//
// Function grouping: door = types, bit-pack utilities, and the translation/record
// builders (the "active logic"). Sibling = codon decoding and AA property tables
// (the "reference data"). Defensible: both are pure lookup tables over Int keys.
//
// Trade-off vs full split (1+5 in handoff_library_split.oot:103-115):
//   - Sibling groups "codon decoding" with "AA properties". Both are reference
//     tables, so the grouping is defensible but less granular than the full split.
//   - Door has ~80 lines of headroom for future additions.
//   - codon_table.oo (ooda/std/bioinformatics/codon_table.oo) is a separate file;
//     not shadowed. handoff_library_split.oot:114-115.
//
// Reversibility: split the sibling into protein_translation_codons.oo (~135 lines)
// and protein_translation_aa.oo (~95 lines) per handoff_library_split.oot:109-111.
// Door stays. Net: 1+1 -> 1+3 (two extra siblings, door unchanged).

// ## 3. dispatch_worker.oo (323 lines, cut >= 67)
//
// Source: ooda/std/swarm/dispatch_worker.oo.
//
// Current shape (file:line):
//   Lines 1-4     Academy header (minimal).
//   Lines 6-12    type DispatcherConfig.
//   Lines 14-23   type SwarmDispatcher.
//   Lines 25-34   type WorkerNode.
//   Lines 36-47   type SwarmTask.
//   Lines 49-80   dispatcher_config_init.
//   Lines 82-93   dispatcher_init.
//   Lines 95-110  worker_node_init.
//   Lines 112-125 swarm_task_create.
//   Lines 127-228 worker_node_can_accept, assign, release, update_status,
//                  heartbeat (102 lines).
//   Lines 230-323 task_is_terminal, can_retry, mark_dispatched, mark_completed,
//                  mark_failed, mark_cancelled (94 lines).
//
// Minimum cut: 1 door + 1 sibling.
//
// | File                              | Role              | Lines  | Budget |
// |-----------------------------------|-------------------|--------|--------|
// | dispatch_worker.oo (door)         | types + worker    | 228    | <=256  |
// | dispatch_worker_task.oo           | task state machine| ~106   | <=256  |
//
// Door (lines 1-228): header + 4 types + 4 ctors + 5 worker ops.
// Sibling body (lines 230-323): 6 task ops.
// Sibling file = 12 (4-element header) + 94 (body) = 106 lines. No imports.
//
// Function grouping: door = the "worker" theme (matches filename dispatch_worker).
// Sibling = task lifecycle, a self-contained state machine. The 6 task ops share
// no internal calls; each is a pure SwarmTask -> SwarmTask transform.
//
// Trade-off vs full split (1+3 in handoff_library_split.oot:148-160):
//   - Door is at 228 lines, only 28 lines of headroom. Future additions to worker
//     ops or types will push it back over 256.
//   - Sibling is small (106 lines) and self-contained; safe from overflow.
//   - Conflict: type DispatcherConfig is declared in dispatch_worker.oo:6-12 AND
//     dispatch_types.oo:6-9 (handoff_library_split.oot:144-146). The minimum cut
//     does NOT dedupe; library lane must address this either now or during upgrade.
//
// Reversibility: split the door into dispatch_worker_types.oo (types + ctors,
// ~135 lines) and dispatch_worker_node.oo (worker ops, ~102 lines) per
// handoff_library_split.oot:153-155. Sibling stays. Net: 1+1 -> 1+3. The dedup
// of DispatcherConfig against dispatch_types.oo is part of this upgrade.

// ## 4. Cross-reference: status stays BLOCKED
//
// All 3 files are in the BLOCKED set per library_status.oot:7 (4476 files, 147 GREEN,
// 568 BLOCKED at last count). BLOCKED cause is oodac gaps, not file size
// (library_status.oot:13-19, handoff_library_split.oot:18-19). The split reduces
// line count only; oodac gap is unchanged.
//
// After the minimum cut:
//   - btree_disk_ops.oo: still BLOCKED, same oodac gap.
//   - protein_translation.oo: still BLOCKED, same oodac gap.
//   - dispatch_worker.oo: still BLOCKED, same oodac gap.
// Audit lane will refresh library_status.oot row entries; expected. Library lane
// must not re-attribute BLOCKED to file size in the new rows
// (handoff_library_split.oot:178).

// ## 5. Acceptance
//
// 1. 3 new sibling .oo files exist:
//      ooda/std/database/btree_disk_ops_mutate.oo
//      ooda/std/bioinformatics/protein_translation_lookup.oo
//      ooda/std/swarm/dispatch_worker_task.oo
// 2. 3 doors slimmed; all <= 256:
//      btree_disk_ops.oo: 225 lines.
//      protein_translation.oo: 173 lines.
//      dispatch_worker.oo: 228 lines.
// 3. 3 new siblings <= 256:
//      btree_disk_ops_mutate.oo: 182 lines.
//      protein_translation_lookup.oo: 217 lines.
//      dispatch_worker_task.oo: 106 lines.
// 4. No new imports beyond originals. btree_disk_ops.oo:13 imports btree_disk_types.oo;
//    the new btree sibling reuses the same. protein_translation.oo and
//    dispatch_worker.oo import nothing; new siblings import nothing.
// 5. 4-element Academy header on each new sibling (FORMAT.oot:31-41).
// 6. oodac check clean on all 6 files (door + sibling for each of 3).
// 7. library_status.oot BLOCKED rows unchanged in cause column.
// 8. All public symbols still importable from the original door path
//    (handoff_library_split.oot:70-73, 119, 162).

// ## 6. Out of scope (per handoff_library_split.oot:180-194)
//
// - Editing btree_disk_types.oo, dispatch_types.oo, codon_table.oo, or any other
//   std file outside the 3 targets.
// - Re-running prove (audit/prove_helpers/* owns prove).
// - Editing library_status.oot or its tails (audit lane owns the door).
// - Renaming public symbols; this is a pure file move, not an API change.
// - DispatcherConfig dedup (handoff_library_split.oot:144-146): deferred to upgrade
//   unless library lane chooses to address it in the minimum cut. The dedup is
//   not required for the 256-line cap.

// ## 7. Summary table
//
// | File                              | Before | Door after | Sibling after | Sibling lines |
// |-----------------------------------|--------|------------|---------------|---------------|
// | btree_disk_ops.oo                 | 395    | 225        | btree_disk_ops_mutate.oo     | 182 |
// | protein_translation.oo            | 380    | 173        | protein_translation_lookup.oo| 217 |
// | dispatch_worker.oo                | 323    | 228        | dispatch_worker_task.oo      | 106 |
//
// All 6 files <= 256. 1+1 for each of 3. Total new files: 3. Net: -3 oversized
// files, +3 siblings. Reversible to the full 1+4 / 1+5 / 1+3 split.
